; A census asks that the rows a pattern sees be the same rows at every
; solution.  While the row (item $v) may or may not be (item a), the census of
; (item a) is undetermined and the rule waits.  Once a rule reads that row as
; (item b), the census sees exactly one row, and the rule fires.
(step one)
(item a) (item $v)
(token)
(rule tally (census (item a)) (absent (tallied)) (make (tallied)))
(rule fix (take (token)) (read (item b)) (make (fixed)))
